-Nested clouds, distance-matrix inputs, representatives and diagram distances
-are not yet part of the public API.
+Nested clouds, distance-matrix inputs, representatives and distances between
+diagram Struct columns are not yet part of the public API.
+
+## Finite bottleneck distance
+
+`polars_tda.finite_bottleneck_distance(left, right)` computes the exact
+L-infinity bottleneck distance between two sequences of finite `(birth, death)`
+pairs, using the existing cocycle Rust solver. Lists and tuples are accepted;
+each pair must have finite endpoints and `birth < death`. Multiplicity is
+preserved. A point can match the diagonal at cost `(death - birth) / 2`.
+Two empty inputs have distance zero. Invalid intervals raise `ValueError`.
+
+This is a scalar helper, not a Polars expression or a consumer of `rips` Structs.
+It releases the GIL during native computation. It copies input pairs into Rust
+intervals and does not establish field, scale or filtration coverage compatibility.
+Callers must handle essential and censored intervals separately; dropping them
+does not establish the distance between the original complete diagrams.
+Exact means no algorithmic approximation, not exact real arithmetic.
+
+```python
+from polars_tda import finite_bottleneck_distance
+
+assert finite_bottleneck_distance([[0.0, 2.0]], [[0.0, 3.0]]) == 1.0
+assert finite_bottleneck_distance([[0.0, 2.0]], []) == 1.0
+```
 
